Create Group 08 — Media & Visual Content for the DevKit.

This group belongs to:

Layer 01 — Foundations & Interface Primitives.

Existing groups:

Group 01 — Interaction Controls
Group 02 — Form Controls
Group 03 — Selection Controls
Group 04 — Navigation Controls
Group 05 — Feedback & Status
Group 06 — Overlays & Surfaces
Group 07 — Data Display

Use the DevKit Core Design Constitution as the immutable global foundation.

Do not redefine global design tokens.

Inherit all existing:
- colors
- semantic colors
- typography
- spacing
- sizing
- control dimensions
- radius
- borders
- elevation
- shadows
- iconography
- motion
- breakpoints
- responsive behavior
- accessibility
- focus treatment
- touch targets
- density
- Light theme
- Dark theme
- High Contrast
- RTL
- localization
- reduced motion
- reduced transparency

Create exactly these 10 components:

071 Image
072 Thumbnail
073 Media Object
074 Icon Container
075 Illustration
076 Cover Media
077 Media Preview
078 Image Placeholder
079 Media Overlay
080 Media Metadata

These are reusable media primitives.

Do not create:
- complete image galleries
- carousels
- complete video players
- image editors
- file managers
- media libraries
- photo grids
- full-screen lightboxes
- complete profile pages
- complete product cards

Those belong to higher-level component groups.

The media system must prioritize:
clarity
correct proportions
fast perception
accessibility
responsive behavior
content integrity

Never distort visual content merely to fit a container.

Support:
natural aspect ratio
fixed aspect ratio
responsive aspect ratio
object-fit behavior
object-position
cropping
containment

The consuming component must be able to choose between:
contain
cover
natural
cropped

Images must not unexpectedly stretch.

Support:
- raster images
- vector illustrations
- thumbnails
- avatars
- previews
- decorative media
- content media

All meaningful images must support alternative text.

Decorative images must be identifiable as decorative.

Do not force alt text onto purely decorative graphics.

When an image fails to load:
provide an appropriate fallback.

Do not display broken-image artifacts as the final visual experience.

Support:
loading
loaded
error
empty
placeholder

Image loading must avoid unnecessary layout shift.

Where dimensions are known:
reserve the appropriate aspect-ratio space before the media loads.

Do not use visual media as the only communication method for important information.

Textual information must remain available where necessary.

Support:
Light
Dark
High Contrast

Media treatments must maintain sufficient contrast for:
labels
overlays
controls
metadata

Do not place white text directly over complex imagery without an appropriate contrast strategy.

Do not add gradients merely for decoration.

If an overlay gradient is used to improve readability:
keep it subtle and purposeful.

Media should feel:
refined,
natural,
high-quality,
balanced,
and content-first.

Avoid:
heavy frames
unnecessary borders
large shadows
excessive rounded containers
decorative gradients
fake glass effects
visual noise

All components must support:

Mobile
Tablet
Desktop
Large Desktop
Ultra Wide

Support:

Mouse
Keyboard
Touch
Stylus
Screen readers

where relevant.

Support:

LTR
RTL
Localization
Dynamic text
Reduced motion
Reduced transparency

Interactive media must have:
visible focus
appropriate semantic behavior
minimum effective touch target

Do not make decorative media interactive.

Do not make every image clickable by default.

Media must remain usable at:
high zoom
large text
narrow screens
wide screens
high contrast

Test:
portrait images
landscape images
square images
extreme aspect ratios
very large images
very small images
missing images
slow-loading images
broken images
transparent images
dark images
bright images
localized metadata
